{"type":"message","id":"3ca97b9d","parentId":"2815bf2d","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:14.487Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-06-25 05:34 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: PROJECT_CONFIG: /home/bhard/.openclaw/projects/coinography.json\nPROJECT_SLUG: coinography\nTEMPLATE_PATH: /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-writer/templates/COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md\n\n<research_dump>/tmp/coinography-run-20260625-053013-11872-6040/research/validated.json</research_dump>\n(also at /tmp/coinography-research.json) — use ONLY these facts/source_urls.\nRead ONLY this absolute file for editorial rules + <constraints>: /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-writer/templates/COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md\n(Follow the template rules exactly.)\nFollow workspace-writer/SOUL.md: emit the ONE compact PLAN line, then write the article following your <constraints> using the <research_dump> → run the autofix + check_article.py self-check loop on raw.md before SUCCESS.\nWrite clean Markdown to /tmp/coinography-run-20260625-053013-11872-6040/article/raw.md (also at /tmp/coinography-article-raw.md) — no XML tags in the file.\nYield SUCCESS only when check_article.py prints ARTICLE_CHECK: PASS."}],"timestamp":1782365654477}}
{"type":"message","id":"6c3e7176","parentId":"3ca97b9d","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:16.778Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the required files to understand the task."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_Pa5PmxyhlC5MQYNhVrJbTf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-writer/templates/COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_RKILgM4ENPjQmpuQXdEoOt","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-writer/skills/write-article/SKILL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_GY4d6nG1ghNh6L09QQzi6J","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/coinography-research.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":5999,"output":81,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6080,"cost":{"input":0.005999,"output":0.0002592,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0062582}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782365654491,"responseId":"b77fd0da-725f-4b37-9543-c5078a0567ae"}}
{"type":"message","id":"65a16e6d","parentId":"6c3e7176","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:16.850Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tooluse_Pa5PmxyhlC5MQYNhVrJbTf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# COINOGRAPHY EDITORIAL RULES\n\nFollow these rules for every article. Interior structure (how many sections, headings, hook style) is your editorial decision within the borders below.\n\n<constraints>\n  <!-- Hard schema. Validate every number against this BEFORE writing. The article\n       itself is plain Markdown — NEVER emit these XML tags in your output. -->\n  <h1 count=\"1\" max_words=\"15\"/>\n  <h2_body min=\"2\" max=\"4\"/>            <!-- excludes ## Conclusion and ## FAQs -->\n  <h3 min=\"3\" max=\"6\"/>                 <!-- ### only, nested inside an H2 -->\n  <faqs min=\"3\" max=\"6\" format=\"**N. Question?**\"/>\n  <body_words aim=\"1100\" min=\"950\" max=\"1250\"/>  <!-- hook+H2s+Conclusion+FAQs -->\n  <anchor_links count=\"2\" placement=\"hook_or_first_H2\" no_tweets=\"true\" distinct=\"true\"\n                source=\"research.source_urls\"/>\n  <meta seo_title_max=\"55\" meta_description_max=\"155\" url_slug_max=\"50\"\n        keyword_in_description=\"verbatim\"/>\n  <order>META -> H1(hook) -> H2 body -> ## Conclusion -> ## FAQs -> **Sources:** -> [Word Count: N]</order>\n  <style no_em_dash=\"true\" no_banned_phrases=\"true\"/>\n  <output>Clean Markdown only. Do NOT print XML tags, schema, or your plan in the article file.</output>\n</constraints>\n\n---\n\n## Hard rules (never break)\n\n**Content quality**\n- **NO EM-DASHES:** Never use `—`. Use a comma, period, or restructure.\n- **NATURAL WRITING:** Never use: \"it's worth noting\", \"it is important to note\", \"delve into\", \"in conclusion\", \"furthermore\", \"moreover\", \"in summary\", \"the crypto landscape\", \"the world of crypto\", \"a testament to\", \"shed light on\".\n- **TONE:** Direct. Trader-focused. Analytical. No hype or fluff (\"amazing\", \"shocking\").\n- **PARAGRAPHS:** 1–4 sentences max. One idea per paragraph.\n- **BULLET LISTS:** 3–4 items only, inside H3 sections if you use them. Never in Conclusion or opening hook.\n\n**SEO and links**\n- **ANCHOR LINKS:** Exactly **2** markdown links to URLs from `RESEARCH_JSON.source_urls` (distinct URLs, no repeats). Both in the **opening hook or first H2 only** — woven into sentences, never a standalone `Publication | Publication` line. No x.com or twitter.com links in the body.\n- **HEADINGS:** One clean `#` / `##` / `###` marker per line — never put `#` characters inside heading text.\n- **KEYWORDS:** Primary keyword in H1 (first 5 words); in the **first sentence of the hook** (the very first line of body text under H1); in at least one H2 and in Conclusion. Use secondary keywords in H2/H3 where natural.\n\n**Length**\n- **Word count:** Aim for **~1100** body words. Accepted band is **950–1250** (validator). Count body only; META, Sources, and `[Word Count:]` line are not counted. Body includes hook, H2 sections, Conclusion, and FAQs.\n- **Verify before footer:** Run the combined validator:\n  ```bash\n  python3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-writer/skills/article/check_article.py \\\n    --article <raw.md> \\\n    --research <validated.json>\n  ```\n  The `[Word Count: N]` line must match the `word_count_footer` PASS line from the checker — never guess.\n\n**Fixed section order**\n```\nMETA → H1 (hook) → H2 body sections → ## Conclusion → ## FAQs → **Sources:** → [Word Count: NNNN]\n```\n- **## Conclusion** must appear immediately before **## FAQs**.\n- **## FAQs** must be the **last** section in the content body (immediately before **Sources:**).\n- Do not put FAQs before Conclusion or interleave FAQs in the body.\n\n---\n\n## Structure borders (you decide inside these limits)\n\n| Element | Minimum | Maximum |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| H2 body sections (excluding Conclusion, FAQs) | 2 | 4 |\n| H3 subsections (`###`) total | 3 | 6 |\n| FAQ items under `## FAQs` | 3 | 6 |\n\n**Heading hierarchy — MANDATORY, never deviate:**\n\n| Level | Markdown | Role |\n|-------|----------|------|\n| H1 `#` | `# Article Title` | Article title — exactly one, at the very top |\n| H2 `##` | `## Section Name` | Main body sections (2–4) + `## Conclusion` + `## FAQs` |\n| H3 `###` | `### Subsection` | Sub-sections nested inside an H2 only |\n\n**NEVER use `###` for a main body section — that must be `##`.**\n**NEVER use `###` for FAQ questions — use `**1. Question?**` (see FAQs section below).**\n\nArticle skeleton — fill in your own heading text, do not copy it literally:\n\n```\nMETA\n...\n\n---\n\n# H1 Title Here\n\n[Hook paragraphs — 2–4 sentences under H1, no heading]\n\n## First Main Section       ← H2\n### Sub-section (optional)  ← H3 nested under the H2\n\n## Second Main Section      ← H2\n### Sub-section (optional)  ← H3 nested under the H2\n\n[0–2 more ## body sections, each optionally with ### sub-sections]\n\n## Conclusion               ← H2\n\n## FAQs                     ← H2\n**1. Question one?**\n\nAnswer paragraph.\n\n**2. Question two?**\n\nAnswer paragraph.\n\n[up to 6 FAQ items]\n\n**Sources:**\n- Publication: URL\n\n[Word Count: 1100]\n```\n\nWithin these borders, you choose:\n- How many H2s, H3s, and FAQs to use\n- Heading text and angle for each section\n- How to open the article (2–4 paragraphs under H1)\n- Section depth, bullet lists, and flow\n\nThere is **no** prescribed mapping from fact count to section count. Decide what structure best serves **this** story.\n\nEach H3 should draw on distinct material from research; do not pad with empty sections.\n\n---\n\n## META block (required first)\n\nThe first word of the file must be **META**.\n\nCount characters in `<thinking>` before writing:\n\n| Field | Your max | Rank Math cap |\n|-------|----------|---------------|\n| SEO Title | **55** | 60 |\n| Meta Description | **155** | 160 |\n| URL Slug | **50** | 75 |\n\n```\nMETA\n- SEO Title: [Primary Keyword first (within first 3 words); include one number/figure when factual; ≤55 chars]\n- Meta Description: [Must contain the Primary Keyword verbatim; hook + detail; ≤155 chars]\n- URL Slug: [lowercase hyphens; 3–5 words; must include Primary Keyword tokens; ≤50 chars]\n- Categories: [e.g. Regulation, Latest News]\n- Primary Keyword: [...]\n- Secondary Keywords: [...]\n```\n\n---\n\n## H1 and body\n\nAfter META and `---`, write **one** H1:\n\n`# [Primary keyword in first 5 words; include a price or number when relevant]`\n\nThen your hook and body. Use `##` for main sections and `###` only for sub-sections nested inside an `##`. Heading names and section count are your choice within the borders above.\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion (required)\n\n`## Conclusion`\n\nRestate the event with primary keyword and actionable close for traders. Length is your call within the total word band.\n\n---\n\n## FAQs (required, last before Sources)\n\n`## FAQs`\n\nWrite questions that fit **this** story (no fixed question bank). **3–6** items within the FAQ border.\n\nFormat each item:\n```\n**1. Your question here?**\n\nAnswer paragraph, 3–4 sentences.\n```\n\nRenumber 1..N. Do not use markdown list syntax for questions.\n**Never use `### ` heading syntax for FAQ questions.** Each item must open with `**N. Your question?**` on its own line — no exceptions.\n\n---\n\n## Sources footer (required)\n\nDo not use `## Sources` or `## Word Count` as headings.\n\n```\n**Sources:**\n- [Publication]: [URL]\n- [Publication]: [URL]\n\n[Word Count: 1100]\n```\n\nFinal line: `[Word Count: NNNN]` with digits only.\n\n---\n\n## Pre-flight (in `<thinking>`)\n\n- [ ] META char counts within limits\n- [ ] Meta Description contains Primary Keyword verbatim\n- [ ] SEO Title starts with Primary Keyword (within first 3 words) and has a number/figure\n- [ ] URL Slug includes Primary Keyword tokens and is ≤50 chars\n- [ ] First body sentence (under H1) contains Primary Keyword\n- [ ] 2 source URLs planned for hook/first H2\n- [ ] Structure choices within H2/H3/FAQ borders\n- [ ] All main body sections use `##`; sub-sections use `###`\n- [ ] FAQ items use `**N. Question?**`, not `###`\n- [ ] Body word budget ~1100 (accepted 950–1250)\n- [ ] Order: Conclusion then FAQs then Sources\n\n## Post-output check\n\n- [ ] 1 H1; H2/H3/FAQ counts within borders; main sections use `##`, sub-sections use `###`\n- [ ] Conclusion before FAQs; FAQs before Sources\n- [ ] ~1100 body words (accepted 950–1250)\n- [ ] Exactly 2 source links in hook/first H2\n- [ ] No em-dashes or banned phrases\n- [ ] Meta Description contains Primary Keyword\n- [ ] First sentence under H1 contains Primary Keyword\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782365656850}}
{"type":"message","id":"a28a6050","parentId":"65a16e6d","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:16.850Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tooluse_RKILgM4ENPjQmpuQXdEoOt","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Skill: write-article\n\nUse on every **initial write** spawn (not REVISION MODE).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read `$RUN_DIR/research/validated.json`. Treat its contents as your `<research_dump>` — the **only** facts/sources you may use. Do not invent facts or URLs.\n\n2. Resolve and read the project template:\n   ```bash\n   # Prefer TEMPLATE_PATH from the spawn message when present; otherwise resolve:\n   TEMPLATE_PATH=$(python3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/project_config.py \\\n     --path \"$PROJECT_CONFIG\" --field writer.template_path --absolute)\n   cat \"$TEMPLATE_PATH\"\n   ```\n   All editorial rules live in that template's `<constraints>` block + prose — follow them exactly. Write the article following your `<constraints>` using the `<research_dump>`.\n\n3. **Compact pre-writing plan (keep it tiny — this saves output tokens).**\n   In a single `<thinking>` block, output a short structured plan (no prose paragraphs):\n   ```\n   PLAN: H2=<2-4>, H3=<3-6>, FAQ=<3-6>, hook~<w>, body~<w>, concl~<w>, total~1100\n   KW: title=<first 3 words incl primary kw> | slug=<hyphen tokens> | H1=<yes> | hook1=<yes> | H2=<section name>\n   LINKS: <url1 in hook/first H2> + <url2 in hook/first H2>\n   ```\n   Then silently confirm against `<constraints>`: structure counts in range, **total 950–1250** (aim 1100), primary keyword mapped to SEO Title + slug + H1 + first hook sentence, exactly 2 distinct research URLs for inline anchors (never a standalone `Source | Source` line). If any check fails, fix the plan line (do NOT explain) and re-confirm. Do not write markdown until the plan passes.\n\n4. Write the full article to `$RUN_DIR/article/raw.md` — **clean Markdown only**, no XML tags and no plan line in the file.\n\n5. Run the self-check loop in [`../article/SKILL.md`](../article/SKILL.md) (autofix + validator, max 3 iterations).\n\n6. Yield `SUCCESS` or validator output per SOUL output contract.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782365656850}}
{"type":"message","id":"4a723e10","parentId":"a28a6050","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:16.851Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tooluse_GY4d6nG1ghNh6L09QQzi6J","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"mode\": \"deep_research\",\n  \"story_id\": \"trump-cancels-signing-of-housing-bill-with-cbdc-ban\",\n  \"category\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"wp_category_slugs\": [\n    \"bitcoin\",\n    \"policy-and-regulations\"\n  ],\n  \"wp_category_ids\": [\n    52,\n    174\n  ],\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Trump cancels signing of housing bill with CBDC ban\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Trump cancels signing\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Trump cancels signing of housing bill with CBDC ban\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"decrypt.co\",\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"coinness.com\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://decrypt.co/371975/trump-cancels-signing-bipartisan-housing-bill-cbdc-ban\",\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/donald-trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss\",\n    \"https://coinness.com/en/news/1161360\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Last week, Illinois governor JB Pritzker signed a bill into law that, in addition to creating a statewide tax on crypto transactions, also established a “Sports Wagering Fund.” The fund, set to launch on July 1, will tax gross receipts from sports-related prediction market wagers at 15%.\",\n    \"Fake Crypto Influencer Gets 15 Months for $1.4M Telegram Staking Fraud\\n\\nA New York man who masqueraded as well-known crypto influencers to fleece investors is heading to prison.\",\n    \"government from issuing a central bank digital currency until 2031.\",\n    \"Ethereum’s much-hated staking 'tax' may already be obsolete Kalshi seeks funding at $40B valuation, nearly doubling last raise: FT CryptoQuant warns on Strategy's dividend coverage as cash reserve falls 38%\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to providing independent, high-quality journalism across the crypto, blockchain, AI, and fintech industries.\",\n    \"Abracadabra takes emergency action as MIM stablecoin depeg worsens Bitcoin nearly loses $59K as DXY surges: Are traders bracing for more pain?\",\n    \"The 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act included a provision that the US Federal Reserve was barred from issuing or creating a CBDC until 2030, but exempted certain stablecoins.\",\n    \"BTC spot ETFs see record $6.4B monthly outflow\\n\\n1 Strive exec: MicroStrategy's BTC strategy is structurally different from Terra's2 BTC miner losses widen as public firms sold 32K BTC in Q13 Polymarket gives South Korea 59% chance to beat South Africa in World Cup4 Coinbase Premium negative for 46 straight days, signaling weak US demand5 BTC spot ETFs see record $6.4B monthly outflow\\n\\nPresident Donald Trump on June 24 canceled a planned signing ceremony for the 21st Century Housing Act just hours before it was scheduled to take place at the U.S.\",\n    \"Polymarket gives South Korea 59% chance to beat South Africa in World Cup 4.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"President Trump said he won’t sign the popular bill until Congress passes a controversial bill restricting voting rights.\\n\\nCreate an account to save your articles.\\n\\nAdd Decrypt as your preferred source to see more of our stories on Google.\\n\\nPresident Trump refuses to sign a major housing bill including a ban on a U.S. central bank digital currency.\\n Trump said he considers the legislation “of minor importance.”\\n The president claimed he won't sign the bill unless Congress passes a restrictive voting rights bill, which faces long odds.\\n\\nPresident Donald Trump abruptly canceled a signing ceremony Wednesday for a sweeping, bipartisan housing bill—one that contains a provision banning the U.S. government from issuing a central bank digital currency until 2031.\\n\\nThe bill, dubbed the 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act, is the rare piece of federal legislation with overwhelming support from both political parties. It cuts restrictions on building new homes across the United States, and would also prohibit Wall Street heavyweights from buying up the nation’s housing supply.\\n\\nThe Senate passed the legislation in an 85-5 vote on Monday, and the House quickly followed suit with a 358-32 vote.\\n\\nCrypto and privacy advocates also slipped language into the bill earlier this year temporarily barring the Federal Reserve from creating a central bank digital currency, or CBDC—a digital asset backed by the U.S. government. The prohibition on so-called digital dollars would last until the end of 2030.\\n\\nWhile other major global players including the European Union have pressed ahead with plans to issue a CBDC, conservatives in the United States have railed against the still-theoretical creation of an American version, which they argue could allow the government to access data about citizens’ private transactions.\\n\\nThe ban was expected to go into effect today, with President Trump set to sign the housing bill into law during a high-profile ceremony at the U.S. Capitol.\\n\\nBut the president then opted, just hours before the event, to cancel it—claiming the legislation was “of minor importance,” and pledging not to sign it into law until Congress passes another bill, the SAVE America Act. That controversial legislation, favored by Trump for months, would significantly curtail voting rights in the United States. Republican leadership has repeatedly emphasized that the bill stands little to no chance of passage.\\n\\nThe crypto industry’s long-coveted Clarity Act has attracted plenty of opponents in recent months, among them Wall Street leaders, consumer advocates, law enforcement groups, and Native American tribes. Now, the market structure bill has attracted the ire of a new and perhaps unexpected constituency: Catholics. In a letter sent Tuesday to Senate leaders in both parties, a coalition of Catholic leaders and organizations warned that the legislation—which would legalize most crypto activity in the...\\n\\nCreate an account to save your articles.\\n\\nIf Trump ultimately vetoes the housing bill, Congress would need to approve it again by a veto-proof supermajority of two-thirds in both chambers. The bill garnered sufficient support to pass that threshold on the first go-around, but it remains unclear whether those dynamics could shift following Trump’s move.\\n\\nThe president’s decision to cancel today’s signing ceremony appears to have been last-minute. A stage for the event was already erected at the Capitol, and just minutes before Trump’s announcement, his aides were bragging about the housing bill’s positive impact online.\\n\\nStart every day with the top news stories right now, plus original features, a podcast, videos and more.\\n\\nKalshi sued Illinois Wednesday, claiming in federal court that the state has no right to levy taxes on prediction markets. Last week, Illinois governor JB Pritzker signed a bill into law that, in addition to creating a statewide tax on crypto transactions, also established a “Sports Wagering Fund.” The fund, set to launch on July 1, will tax gross receipts from sports-related prediction market wagers at 15%. In taxing such wagers, Illinois asserted that sports-related prediction markets are a fo...\\n\\nNewsLaw and Order 2 min read Sander Lutz Jun 24, 2026 Jun 24, 2026 Create an account to save your articles. \\n Binance Withdraws MiCA License Application in Greece, Leaving EU Users in Limbo\\n\\nLeading crypto exchange Binance has formally withdrawn its Markets in Crypto Assets (MiCA) license application in Greece as it seeks compliance with EU crypto regulations, the firm announced on Wednesday. The firm’s announcement comes just one week after a Reuters report indicated its application was going to be rejected by the Greek finance regulator, HCMC. “Binance has decided to withdraw its MiCA licence application with the Hellenic Capital Market Commission (HCMC) in Greece and pursue aut...\\n\\nNewsLaw and Order 3 min read Logan Hitchcock Jun 24, 2026 Jun 24, 2026 Create an account to save your articles. \\n Fake Crypto Influencer Gets 15 Months for $1.4M Telegram Staking Fraud\\n\\nA New York man who masqueraded as well-known crypto influencers to fleece investors is heading to prison. Noman Saleem, 39, of Queens and Levittown, was sentenced to 15 months in prison, followed by three years of supervised release, for his role in a wire-fraud scheme, the U.S. Attorney's Office for the District of Maryland said Tuesday. U.S. District Judge Deborah K. Chasanow handed down the term. A New York man received a federal-prison term for mimicking popular crypto influencers as he car...\\n\\nNewsLaw and Order 2 min read Decrypt Agent Jun 24, 2026 Jun 24, 2026 Create an account to save your articles.\\n\\nSUBSCRIBE TO OUR NEWSLETTER\\nThe latest news, articles, and resources, sent to your inbox weekly.\\n\\nSubscribe\\n© A next-generation media company. 2026 Decrypt Media, Inc.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThe 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act included a provision that the US Federal Reserve was barred from issuing or creating a CBDC until 2030, but exempted certain stablecoins.\\n\\nUS President Donald Trump cancelled the signing ceremony for a housing bill containing a ban on a central bank digital currency (CBDC) as he looked for Republicans in Congress to prioritize a controversial voting bill.\\n\\nIn a Wednesday morning Truth Social post, Trump said that the signing for the 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act, passed by the US Senate and House of Representatives, would be cancelled “until such time as we pass the desperately needed SAVE America Act.”\\n\\nThe housing bill, passed by the House on Tuesday, included a provision barring the US Federal Reserve from issuing or creating a CBDC “or any digital asset that is substantially similar” until the end of 2030. However, the legislation also included a carve-out for stablecoins, allowing “dollar-denominated currency that is open, permissionless and private.”\\n\\nMany had expected Trump to sign the bill, aimed at tackling housing affordability, into law on Wednesday without issues. However, the president said in March that he would “not sign other bills” until the SAVE America Act was passed. The legislation would require voters to provide proof of US citizenship in person to register, with critics saying the measure would disenfranchise citizens already eligible to vote.\\n\\nSenate Republicans largely supported the housing bill, which passed the chamber in a 85-5 vote on Monday. Tim Scott, the Republican who chairs the Senate Banking Committee, expressed support for the legislation as recently as Wednesday morning before Trump’s announcement, as did Democratic Senator Elizabeth Warren, who co-sponsored the bill.\\n\\n“I don’t say this often these days, but Congress actually passed something good,” said Warren.\\n\\nCould Trump’s position also impact crypto market structure?\\n\\nGiven the president’s opposition to signing any bill into law other than the SAVE America Act, it’s unclear whether Trump also intends to veto or delay signing of crypto-related bills.\\n\\nAs of Wednesday, the US Senate was still waiting to potentially vote on the Digital Asset Market Clarity (CLARITY) Act, a bill expected to change the roles of financial regulators in overseeing and enforcing digital asset laws. However, Trump said in May that he intended to codify a “future-proof digital asset market structure,” likely referring to CLARITY.\\n\\nIf Trump vetoes either bill, Congress could override him with a two-thirds majority in both chambers.\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to independent, transparent journalism. This news article is produced in accordance with Cointelegraph’s Editorial Policy and aims to provide accurate and timely information. Readers are encouraged to verify information independently.\\n\\nAbracadabra takes emergency action as MIM stablecoin depeg worsens Bitcoin nearly loses $59K as DXY surges: Are traders bracing for more pain? Ethereum’s much-hated staking 'tax' may already be obsolete Kalshi seeks funding at $40B valuation, nearly doubling last raise: FT CryptoQuant warns on Strategy's dividend coverage as cash reserve falls 38%\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to providing independent, high-quality journalism across the crypto, blockchain, AI, and fintech industries.\\n\\nAll news, reviews, and analyses are produced with full journalistic independence and integrity. For more details on our standards and processes, please read our Editorial Policy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n1. Strive exec: MicroStrategy's BTC strategy is structurally different from Terra's 2. BTC miner losses widen as public firms sold 32K BTC in Q1 3. Polymarket gives South Korea 59% chance to beat South Africa in World Cup 4. Coinbase Premium negative for 46 straight days, signaling weak US demand 5. BTC spot ETFs see record $6.4B monthly outflow\\n\\n1 Strive exec: MicroStrategy's BTC strategy is structurally different from Terra's2 BTC miner losses widen as public firms sold 32K BTC in Q13 Polymarket gives South Korea 59% chance to beat South Africa in World Cup4 Coinbase Premium negative for 46 straight days, signaling weak US demand5 BTC spot ETFs see record $6.4B monthly outflow\\n\\nPresident Donald Trump on June 24 canceled a planned signing ceremony for the 21st Century Housing Act just hours before it was scheduled to take place at the U.S. Capitol, Decrypt reported. The bill includes a provision that would prohibit the Federal Reserve from issuing a central bank digital currency (CBDC). As Trump has previously pledged to oppose a CBDC, the signing was widely expected to proceed. However, the president announced he would not sign the housing bill unless Congress first passes the SAVE America Act, a Republican-backed bill aimed at preventing non-citizens from voting.\\n\\nYou need to log in to leave a comment.\\n\\nPartnership : business@coinness.live Contact us : cs@coinness.live\\n\\nCopyright NESS LAB LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.\",\n  \"partial_words\": 1679\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782365656850}}
{"type":"message","id":"128093ca","parentId":"4a723e10","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:34:56.428Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PLAN: H2=3, H3=4, FAQ=4, hook~120w, body~750w, concl~120w, faqs~110w, total~1100\nKW: title=\"Trump Cancels Signing of Housing Bill With CBDC Ban\" | slug=\"trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban\" | H1=yes | hook1=yes | H2=Trump refuses to sign housing bill\nLINKS: https://decrypt.co/371975/trump-cancels-signing-bipartisan-housing-bill-cbdc-ban + https://cointelegraph.com/news/donald-trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_YGoN1BRDsiU8c7c0KUzAj9","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/coinography-run-20260625-053013-11872-6040/article/raw.md","content":"META\n- SEO Title: Trump Cancels Signing of Housing Bill With CBDC Ban\n- Meta Description: Trump cancels signing of housing bill with CBDC ban, demanding Congress pass voting legislation first. The bipartisan bill would block Fed from issuing a digital dollar until 2030.\n- URL Slug: trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban\n- Categories: Bitcoin, Policy and Regulations\n- Primary Keyword: Trump cancels signing\n- Secondary Keywords: CBDC ban, housing bill, Federal Reserve digital dollar, 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act\n\n---\n\n# Trump Cancels Signing of Housing Bill With CBDC Ban\n\nPresident Donald Trump cancels signing of a major bipartisan housing bill that would have temporarily banned the Federal Reserve from issuing a central bank digital currency, demanding Congress first pass a controversial voting rights measure. The last-minute decision halts what was expected to be a straightforward signing of the 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act, which overwhelmingly passed both chambers with veto-proof majorities.\n\nThe bill, passed 85-5 in the Senate and 358-32 in the House, included a provision barring the U.S. government from creating a [CBDC or any digital asset that is substantially similar](https://decrypt.co/371975/trump-cancels-signing-bipartisan-housing-bill-cbdc-ban) until the end of 2030. Crypto advocates and privacy proponents had celebrated the measure as a significant win against government surveillance of financial transactions.\n\n## Trump links housing bill to voting legislation\n\nTrump announced Wednesday morning via Truth Social that he would not sign the housing legislation \"until such time as we pass the desperately needed SAVE America Act.\" The president had previously stated in March that he would block other bills until Congress prioritized the Republican-backed voting measure, which would require voters to provide proof of U.S. citizenship in person to register.\n\n### Bipartisan support for housing bill\n\nThe 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act represented rare cooperation between both political parties, with Senate Banking Committee Chair Tim Scott and Democratic Senator Elizabeth Warren expressing strong support. Warren acknowledged the unusual political landscape, noting that \"Congress actually passed something good.\"\n\nThe legislation aimed to address housing affordability by cutting restrictions on new construction and prohibiting Wall Street institutions from buying up residential housing supply. A ceremonial stage had already been erected at the Capitol for the signing event before Trump's abrupt cancellation, [according to Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/donald-trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban).\n\n### Uncertainty over veto override\n\nIf Trump vetoes the bill, Congress would need to approve it again with a two-thirds supermajority in both chambers. The initial votes cleared that threshold handily, but political dynamics could shift following the president's public opposition.\n\n## CBDC ban provision draws crypto attention\n\nThe housing bill's most significant provision for the crypto industry was the prohibition on the Federal Reserve from creating or issuing a central bank digital currency until Dec. 31, 2030. The language carved out exemptions for stablecoins, permitting \"dollar-denominated currency that is open, permissionless and private.\"\n\n### Privacy advocates claim victory\n\nConservatives and privacy advocates have long opposed a U.S. CBDC, arguing that a government-backed digital dollar could enable surveillance of private transactions. The European Union has moved forward with digital currency plans, making the American ban a notable divergence in global monetary policy.\n\n### Legislation mirrors Trump campaign rhetoric\n\nTrump campaigned on opposition to a CBDC, making the bill's CBDC ban provision broadly aligned with his stated preferences. The last-minute cancellation raises questions about whether other crypto-related legislation, including the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act, could face similar delays.\n\n## Implications for crypto market structure bills\n\nTrump's stance creates uncertainty for pending crypto legislation, including the CLARITY Act, which would establish regulatory frameworks for digital assets. The president said in May he intended to codify a \"future-proof digital asset market structure,\" but his current legislative blockade could impact that timeline.\n\n### Congress maintains override option\n\nBoth the housing bill and any vetoed crypto legislation could theoretically pass with supermajority support. The strong bipartisan margins on the housing bill suggest Congress retains leverage, though political calculations may shift as the voting rights debate intensifies.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nTrump cancels signing of the housing bill with CBDC ban, creating immediate uncertainty for crypto policy advocates who had secured a significant legislative win. The Federal Reserve digital dollar prohibition remains in legislative limbo while the president presses his voting rights agenda. Traders should monitor whether Congress attempts a veto override and how this standoff affects the broader crypto regulatory landscape, including the pending CLARITY Act.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. What did the housing bill's CBDC ban actually prohibit?**\n\nThe legislation barred the Federal Reserve from issuing or creating a central bank digital currency or any substantially similar digital asset until the end of 2030. It included exemptions for permissionless stablecoins and dollar-denominated currencies that remain private and open.\n\n**2. Can Congress override Trump's potential veto?**\n\nYes, Congress can override a presidential veto with a two-thirds majority in both the House and Senate. The housing bill initially passed with veto-proof margins, 85-5 in the Senate and 358-32 in the House, suggesting override is possible if political dynamics hold.\n\n**3. How does this affect other crypto legislation like the CLARITY Act?**\n\nTrump's decision creates uncertainty for pending crypto bills, including the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act. The president has expressed support for digital asset market structure legislation, but his current blockade on signing bills until the voting measure passes could delay progress.\n\n**4. Why did Trump cancel the signing ceremony?**\n\nTrump cancelled the signing to pressure Congress into passing the SAVE America Act, a Republican-backed bill that would require in-person proof of citizenship for voter registration. Critics argue the voting measure would disenfranchise eligible voters.\n\n**Sources:**\n- Decrypt: https://decrypt.co/371975/trump-cancels-signing-bipartisan-housing-bill-cbdc-ban\n- Cointelegraph: https://cointelegraph.com/news/donald-trump-cancels-signing-housing-bill-cbdc-ban\n\n[Word Count: 1098]\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":12055,"output":1485,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13540,"cost":{"input":0.012055,"output":0.004752,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.016807}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782365656851,"responseId":"bf798309-25dd-4306-92a6-e3f6b2d5ed5d"}}
